```php
$fp = fopen("php://temp", "a+");
fwrite($fp, "hello");
fseek($fp, 0, SEEK_SET);
fwrite($fp, "world");
echo stream_get_contents($fp, -1, 0);
```

php answers `helloworld`. elephc answered `world` — the first write was gone, in
silence, on a stream php guarantees can only grow. php's `a` modes send every
write to the END whatever `fseek()` did, which is the entire point of asking for
one, and code that seeks around an append-mode buffer therefore lost data rather
than accumulating it.

